"a+" Mode — Easy Explanation
What does "append" mean?

Append = add to the end without deleting existing data
Think of a file as a notebook.

When you use:

open("file.txt", "a+")

Python does 3 things:

✅ Opens the file for reading
✅ Opens the file for writing
✅ Adds new data at the end of the file (append)
✅ Creates the file if it doesn't already exist